{
    "name": "E2E SAP Emarsys - New Customer Trigger",
    "description": "End-to-end harness for the SAP Emarsys New Customer trigger - the event has to be provoked by hand from an Automation Center program.",
    "notes": {
        "8484f30f-3054-434d-bc0f-18792a91c406": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 32,
            "width": 928,
            "height": 208,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Manual provoke required - Emarsys cannot register a webhook through its API\n\nThe only push mechanism Emarsys offers is the Automation Center **Webhook node**, which a human\nconfigures in the Emarsys UI. This flow is therefore a repeatable manual verification harness,\nnot an unattended test.\n\n1. Start the flow, open the **New Customer** node and copy the read-only **Webhook URL**.\n2. In Emarsys go to Automation > Webhook Node Presets and create a preset that POSTs to that URL.\n   Add the contact data keys `contact_id` and `email` to the preset - the Assert checks both.\n3. Build an audience-based program with the **New Contact** entry point, a short wait, and that\n   webhook node, then activate it and let a contact enter it (or send the preset test delivery).\n4. \"Load All Contact Fields\" is on, so the credential also needs `contact.getdata` and `field.list`.\n5. Pause the Emarsys program before you stop this flow, otherwise the program drops into fail-safe\n   mode after repeated delivery failures.\n\nThe OnStart -> Wait lane only keeps the flow busy while you click through Emarsys - do not remove it.\nAfterAll waits 600 s for the delivery."
        }
    },
